#### Signal Space Separation

Signal-space separation (SSS)
({{ ref('TauluKajola2005', 'Samu Taulu and Matti Kajola. Presentation of electromagnetic multichannel data: the signal space separation method. *Journal of Applied Physics*, 97(12):124905, 2005. doi:10.1063/1.1935742') }},
{{ ref('TauluSimola2006', 'Samu Taulu and Juha Simola. Spatiotemporal signal space separation method for rejecting nearby interference in MEG measurements. *Physics in Medicine and Biology*, 51(7):1759–1768, 2006. doi:10.1088/0031-9155/51/7/008') }}),
implemented in MNE-Python
({{ ref('Gramfort2014', 'Gramfort, A., Luessi, M., Larson, E., Engemann, D. A., Strohmeier, D., Brodbeck, C., ... & Hämäläinen, M. S. (2014). MNE software for processing MEG and EEG data. *NeuroImage*, 86, 446–460. doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2013.10.027') }}),
was applied separately to each recording block to identify bad MEG channels, reconstruct them during SSS, and suppress external magnetic interference.
